&lt;img src="http://web.archive.org/web/20150414144207im_/http:/lichtspielhaus3d.com/img/showings/lichtspielhaus/jpg/small/03.jpg" alt=""&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;img src="http://web.archive.org/web/20150414144207im_/http:/lichtspielhaus3d.com/img/showings/lichtspielhaus/jpg/small/04.jpg" alt=""&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;img src="http://web.archive.org/web/20150414144207im_/http:/lichtspielhaus3d.com/img/showings/lichtspielhaus/jpg/small/05.jpg" alt=""&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;img src="http://web.archive.org/web/20150414144207im_/http:/lichtspielhaus3d.com/img/showings/lichtspielhaus/jpg/small/06.jpg" alt=""&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;img src="http://web.archive.org/web/20150414144207im_/http:/lichtspielhaus3d.com/img/showings/lichtspielhaus/jpg/small/07.jpg" alt=""&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;img src="http://web.archive.org/web/20150414144207im_/http:/lichtspielhaus3d.com/img/showings/lichtspielhaus/jpg/small/08.jpg" alt=""&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Lichtspiele — A Typocalypse Typeface</title><link>https://jolg42.github.io/typophile/113960/</link><pubDate>Thu, 06 Feb 2014 04:36:00 +0100</pubDate><guid>https://jolg42.github.io/typophile/113960/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lichtspiele — A typocalypse display typeface&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Cinemas from the early 20th Century are called &amp;ldquo;Lichtspiele&amp;rdquo; in Germany. &amp;ldquo;Lichtspiele&amp;rdquo; transports you back to a time where neon lights and marquee letters decorated cinema facades.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Of the 5 styles, three have two versions of italics - one for each perspective. Display is your basic style. Neon is inspired by the old neon letters found outside cinemas.&lt;br&gt;
Add Neon Outline to Display or Neon to add another layer to your artwork. Neon 3D is a extruded version of Neon. Screen Credits is based on the liner notes of movie posters.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Font from Gilda movie tittle</title><link>https://jolg42.github.io/typophile/100326/</link><pubDate>Sun, 03 Feb 2013 09:23:00 +0100</pubDate><guid>https://jolg42.github.io/typophile/100326/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Hello guys,&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I quite like the &amp;ldquo;font&amp;rdquo; most likely a hand drawn illustration of the movie tittle from GILDA.&lt;br&gt;
Any suggestions as to what current font might come close?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;thank you,&lt;br&gt;
Rodrigo&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="http://web.archive.org/web/20131011224542im_/http:/typophile.com/files/gilda-title-still_4010.jpeg" alt=""&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Brand NEW! Smoking Club Typeface</title><link>https://jolg42.github.io/typophile/100055/</link><pubDate>Fri, 25 Jan 2013 13:12:00 +0100</pubDate><guid>https://jolg42.github.io/typophile/100055/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Brand NEW!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;New typeface released, it was inspired by movie tittles from old B&amp;amp;W Hollywood movies. The typeface was custom designed in vector format using a high number of colors to produce a realistic 3D effect.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It is perfect for display use, large format graphics, magazines, posters and 3D design.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It was showcased at Typography Served: &lt;a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20150415103000/http:/www.typographyserved.com/gallery/Smoking-Club-Typeface/5410327" title="http://www.typographyserved.com/gallery/Smoking-Club-Typeface/5410327"&gt;http://www.typographyserved.com/gallery/Smoking-Club-Typeface/5410327&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;
